Alice: Ha, yeah, me too. I like to play a lot, but I never gamble. :)

Bob: Yeah, I don't gamble on big games either. Except for one time a few weeks ago.

Alice: A few weeks ago, Joe?

Bob: I went to a friend's house. He wanted to play big games, so I said, "Let's play." He said one cent per card because he plays very well. I said, "So what," because at most I would lose about $10.

Alice: That's good. :) Haha. It's good actually, but if I had to gamble, I wouldn't enjoy the game fully.

Bob: But it's not good to "stand so hard"—if you have to gamble, it's very stressful. By the way, do you have the program?

Alice: My program. It's there, but you need to download it or something. :)

Bob: You need a program to play online. My client doesn't support file transfers yet... maybe you can get it from me via FTP or HTTP... wait...

Alice: Okay. :) I'll get it. Haha. [end of text]


